-- GH-WEBHOOK-INTAKE-1 and GH-APP-FLEET-2 (2026-10-20, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 2582 and 2596). Companion of qnfo-fleet-control 0.44.0 (POST /gh/webhook, POST /gh-app/token, qnfo-fleet-control/gh-webhook.test.mjs).
-- What this file does (INSERT OR IGNORE and guarded UPDATE only): two standing slice contracts (runner-https probes that the two new routes are live on the deployed worker, no issue_id, so passing them never closes
-- an issue early), a PROGRESS note on each issue that names the remainder and its doer (OWNER-NO-LOOSE-ENDS-1: the issue stays open on its own closing probe, a gh-webhook row inside 120 minutes for 2582 and qnfo-ops
-- /health gh_app ok for 2596), and a decision_log row. Measured 2026-10-20 06:2xZ before the change: cloud_ops_events kind gh-webhook 0 rows ever, git grep x-github-event on main 0 matches, qnfo-ops /health has no gh_app field.
-- spof-review: the 10-minute poll of the merge lane (stale-PR lane and code loop) stays the second path of the webhook, so a missed, unsigned or unconfigured delivery costs at most one cycle; the App token broker is read-only and every caller keeps its personal-token fallback, so a failing broker costs nothing a caller had before.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class IN ('slice-gh-webhook-route-live', 'slice-gh-app-broker-live'); UPDATE agent_issues SET description = replace(description, char(10) || 'PROGRESS 2026-10-20 (agent-clusterD-a0676665, qnfo-fleet-control 0.44.0, GH-WEBHOOK-INTAKE-1 route): POST /gh/webhook is built (X-Hub-Signature-256 against the worker secret GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET, 503 and nothing accepted while it is unset, one cloud_ops_events row per delivery of kind gh-webhook, the merge lane run at once for a check_suite that completed with success or a pull request opened, reopened or ready, debounced to one run a minute, the 10-minute poll kept as the second path; gh-webhook.test.mjs). Slice probe (contract slice-gh-webhook-route-live): GET /gh/webhook answers route gh-webhook-intake. Remainder, which is what this issue''s closing probe (a gh-webhook row inside 120 minutes) waits on: (1) the worker secret GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET, set under the secret lock by a loop or session and never printed, and (2) the webhook registered on QNFO/qnfo-workers (payload URL https://qnfo-fleet-control.q08.workers.dev/gh/webhook, JSON, events pull_request, check_suite and push, the same secret) through a webhook action in scripts/github-settings-actions.mjs run by github-settings-actions.yml with QNFO_GH_PAT. A refusal of the repository settings write by that credential is recorded verbatim and handed to the owner as one IDENTITY-BOUND card; until it is refused nothing here is owner-only.', '') WHERE id = 2582; UPDATE agent_issues SET description = replace(description, char(10) || 'PROGRESS 2026-10-20 (agent-clusterD-a0676665, qnfo-fleet-control 0.44.0, GH-APP-FLEET-2 broker route): POST /gh-app/token is built on qnfo-fleet-control: a service binding whose ctx.props.caller is one of the 13 listed workers gets the cached installation token with its expiry (never the personal token, never logged, one audit row per caller and hour), a public host, missing props or an unlisted caller get 403; GET /gh-app reports broker service-binding (gh-webhook.test.mjs). Slice probe (contract slice-gh-app-broker-live): GET /gh-app contains broker service-binding. Remainder, one change per worker, qnfo-ops first: a [[services]] binding to qnfo-fleet-control with props = { caller = "<worker>" } in its wrangler.toml, a ghAppBroker client that POSTs /gh-app/token and caches the token until five minutes before expires_at with the personal token as fallback, and gh_app on its /health; this issue''s closing probe is qnfo-ops /health reading gh_app ok.', '') WHERE id = 2596
